<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<timedtext format="3">
<head>
<pen id="1" b="1" fc="#FFFFFF" fo="254" bc="#140804" bo="170" et="4" ec="#000000" fs="4" sz="120"/>
<pen id="2" b="1" fc="#FFD23A" fo="254" bc="#140804" bo="190" et="4" ec="#000000" fs="4" sz="125"/>
<wp id="1" ap="7" ah="50" av="80"/>
<ws id="1" ju="2"/>
</head>
<body>
<p t="400" d="1650" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="1">Four thousand
two hundred years</s></p>
<p t="2080" d="1890" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="1">ago, a people
descending from the</s></p>
<p t="4000" d="1610" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="1">Zagros mountains toppled
the world's first</s></p>
<p t="5640" d="609" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="1">empire.</s></p>
<p t="6280" d="2170" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="2">The Sumerians fearfully
called them the Dragon</s></p>
<p t="8480" d="1290" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="1">of the Mountains.</s></p>
<p t="9800" d="1530" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="1">They were the Gutians.</s></p>
<p t="11360" d="1250" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="1">They brought the
Akkadian Empire</s></p>
<p t="12640" d="2210" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="1">to its knees and
ruled Mesopotamia for</s></p>
<p t="14880" d="1409" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="1">a full hundred years.</s></p>
<p t="16320" d="1809" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="1">The Sumerian King
List describes them</s></p>
<p t="18160" d="1649" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="1">like this: They were their</s></p>
<p t="19840" d="982" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="1">own kings.</s></p>
<p t="20852" d="1036" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="1">Twenty-one kings, a</s></p>
<p t="21919" d="2410" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="1">tribal council and
local autonomy.</s></p>
<p t="24360" d="1929" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="1">Thousands of years
later, this order</s></p>
<p t="26320" d="1782" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="2">lived on in
Kurdish society.</s></p>
<p t="28133" d="2116" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="1">The name Gutium
never disappeared.</s></p>
<p t="30279" d="1730" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="1">Kurti in Assyrian records,</s></p>
<p t="32040" d="1609" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="1">Kardouchoi in
Xenophon, Corduene</s></p>
<p t="33680" d="2359" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="2">in Roman times, and Kurd</s></p>
<p t="36080" d="689" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="1">today.</s></p>
<p t="36800" d="1369" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="1">According to scholars</s></p>
<p t="38199" d="929" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="1">such as Arshak</s></p>
<p t="39160" d="2143" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="1">Safrastian, Godfrey
Driver, Ephraim Speiser and</s></p>
<p t="41333" d="1877" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="1">Mehrdad Izady, the
Gutians are the</s></p>
<p t="43240" d="1329" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="2">ancestors of the Kurds.</s></p>
<p t="44600" d="1609" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="1">Hurrians,
Mitanni, Lullubi,</s></p>
<p t="46240" d="1769" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="1">Kassites, Medes and</s></p>
<p t="48040" d="1409" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="1">Corduene: all are</s></p>
<p t="49480" d="1649" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="1">the four-thousand-year-old
roots of</s></p>
<p t="51160" d="1289" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="2">the Kurdish people.</s></p>
<p t="52480" d="1517" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="1">Subscribe to
Dîrok and don't</s></p>
<p t="54027" d="1773" wp="1" ws="1"><s p="1">miss the rest
of the story.</s></p>
</body>
</timedtext>
